# Cost discipline

User validates UI on their own pN. Agent verification is the smallest hermetic test for touched paths, then ship per `how-we-work.mdc`.

## Verification off by default

Do not use browser MCP, Playwright, `ux-*.mjs`, or npm scripts matching `test:e2e*` unless this chat explicitly asks.

## Tests before ship

Run only the script for the paths you changed. If several areas changed, run those scripts in sequence. Do not run `test:all`, `test:packages` (whole loop), `security:comprehensive`, `performance:optimize`, or `integration:test`.

| Touched area | Command |
|---|---|
| `apps/aggregator-browser/` | `npm run test:browser:unit` |
| `apps/id-dashboard/` | `npm run test:dashboard:unit` |
| `apps/pen/` | `npm run test:pen` |
| `apps/prism/` or prism API | `npm run test:prism` |
| `api/` | `npm run test:api` |
| `packages/<name>/` | `cd packages/<name> && npm test` |

Rules-only or docs-only edits do not need a package test. Do not run `./deploy.sh` or full monorepo builds unless this chat explicitly asks to deploy.

## Search and tools

Follow `agent-scope.mdc` search scope. No repo-wide grep for UI-only work. Open `diagnostic-discipline.mdc` only for auth, Drive, OAuth, or `ownerFetch`. No WebSearch, Task, subagent, Bugbot, or security-review unless this chat asks. Named paths first; at most one widening search, then ask the user.

## Docs

Prefer code and tests over markdown. Do not Read or grep `docs/archive/**`, `docs/legal/**`, `**/DIAGNOSTIC_*.md`, `**/*REFACTORING*PLAN*.md`, `FIX_PLAN.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `FEED_SYSTEM_PRODUCTION_PLAN.md`, or `BROWSER_REDESIGN_PLAN.md` unless the user `@`-mentions that file. Do not open `SHARED_CODE_RULES.md` unless the task is shared-architecture or the user `@`s it. Live SoTs when needed: `docs/architecture/ADR_*.md`, `docs/architecture/PEN_*_V0.md`, `docs/architecture/overview.md` — named sections only. Index: `docs/README.md`.

## Ship

After the targeted test (or when no test applies): `git add` (no `.env`, secrets, `.local/`, `.firebase`) → commit → push. Do **not** run `./deploy.sh`, `firebase deploy`, or API-host deploy unless this chat explicitly asks. Remind the user once: live hosting updates when they run `./deploy.sh` from the repo root in their terminal.
